{"_key": "roundlog|edge-a NotebookEdit over an existing round log#9e6eb4fe90471d7a", "err": "\u274c BLOCKED: a whole-file write to a pr-babysit round log. Its STATUS block is spliced in place, and the obvious splice (text[:i] + new) deletes the entire round history below it -- which is what happened on 2026-08-19, silently, to a file with no backup. To refresh STATUS use the verb, which replaces ONLY that block and reports the bytes it kept above and below:  .claude/hooks/stop/worklist.py --roundlog <branch> <<'EOF' ... EOF   The tool writes the '## STATUS (round N, <utc>)' heading itself: the round auto-increments, and the stamp is machine-written because a watchdog reads it to decide whether this loop is wedged. To append to the history or amend the wave header, use Edit -- targeted edits are deliberately allowed, because they cannot swallow an appendix they never named.\n", "out": "", "rc": "2"}
